### BizPlay Conversational Agent — manual API tests
### No auth token required (security is permitAll). Default port 8080.
### Run top-to-bottom: request #2 captures the sessionId used by #3 and #4.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@corpNo = 1234567890

### 1) Staff lookup (standalone fixed-path agent) -> POST /staff-lookup
# `name` is optional: provide it to skip LLM extraction; omit it to let the LLM
# pull a name out of `message`.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/agent-conversations/staff-lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "corpNo": "{{corpNo}}",
  "name": "John Doe",
  "message": "who is John Doe"
}

### 2) Create a session -> POST /sessions   (captures sessionId for later calls)
# @name createSession
POST {{host}}/api/v1/agent-conversations/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "corpNo": "{{corpNo}}"
}

### capture the returned UUID for reuse below
@sessionId = {{createSession.response.body.data.sessionId}}

### 3a) Trip-plan chat — STAFF_LOOKUP lane (single person, no filters)
# Matches -> appends a TravelerDraft into draft_json.TripInformation.Travelers
POST {{host}}/api/v1/agent-conversations/trip-plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "corpNo": "{{corpNo}}",
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}",
  "message": "who is John Doe"
}

### 3b) Trip-plan chat — DATABASE_LOOKUP lane (text-to-SQL, filtered/multi-row)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/agent-conversations/trip-plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "corpNo": "{{corpNo}}",
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}",
  "message": "list all staff in the sales department"
}

### 3c) Trip-plan chat — follow-up that relies on session history
POST {{host}}/api/v1/agent-conversations/trip-plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "corpNo": "{{corpNo}}",
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}",
  "message": "also show their past trips to Busan"
}

### 3d) Trip-plan chat — no sessionId (server auto-creates one and returns it)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/agent-conversations/trip-plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "corpNo": "{{corpNo}}",
  "message": "find Jane Smith"
}

### 4) Create a business trip plan -> POST /plans   (full draft skeleton)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/plans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "CorpNo": "{{corpNo}}",
  "PlanType": "Business Trip Plan",
  "Attachemnt": [
    { "Type": "File", "FileID": "FILE_ID_001" },
    { "Type": "URL", "URL": "https://example.com/itinerary.pdf" }
  ],
  "TripInformation": {
    "Purpose": "General Business Trip",
    "BusinessPeriod": "2024-07-01 to 2024-07-05",
    "Destination": "Busan",
    "Title": "Business Trip to Busan",
    "Content": "Meeting with clients and visiting local offices.",
    "Business Trip Classifcation": "CS",
    "Travelers": [
      {
        "Name": "John Doe",
        "Department": "Sales",
        "Position": "Manager",
        "Origin": "Seoul",
        "Destination": "Busan",
        "ReturnPoint": "Seoul"
      },
      {
        "Name": "Jane Smith",
        "Department": "Marketing",
        "Position": "Specialist",
        "Origin": "Seoul",
        "Destination": "Busan",
        "ReturnPoint": "Seoul"
      }
    ]
  }
}
